00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.659
Jack: So, what exactly is a project
manager and what do they do?

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.180
Project management has always been
important in business and is getting

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.360
more so all the time as project
management skills are in more demand.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.730
Project managers are responsible
for overseeing all the processes

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:20.800
we have just looked at, Initiating,
planning, executing, monitoring,

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.529
and controlling and closing.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.650
These are also known as
the ‘project life cycle’.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.889
They don’t do this on their own but
instead are involved in all the different

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:33.810
stages in one capacity or another and
they may not even be assigned to the

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.710
role until the project is underway.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.519
It is their responsibility to make
sure that the right people are

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.120
assigned to the right roles and that
all planning is carried out properly

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.569
to achieve the target outcome.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.779
They will also protect the team
from any distractions and lead them

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.580
through the executing of the project.

00:00:51.139 --> 00:00:54.980
They will also be on top of monitoring
the progress of the project at all stages

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.300
and addressing any issues that may arise.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.660
At closing they will be responsible
for making sure everything has been

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.369
finalised and working with the client
or stakeholders to get everything

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.429
signed off and reviewing the process.

00:01:08.469 --> 00:01:10.529
Let’s hear what it is like
to be a project manager.

